WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.319
Welcome to Rendprop.

00:00:01.319 --> 00:00:12.748
This guide walks through one complete listing: enter the home, capture photos, review optional edits, make a video, publish the website, and follow up with buyers.

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:18.735
The bottom bar has Home, Listings, Activity, Leads, and Account.

00:00:18.735 --> 00:00:20.969
Home starts new work.

00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:23.204
Listings holds each property.

00:00:23.204 --> 00:00:24.880
Activity tracks jobs.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.556
Leads holds enquiries.

00:00:26.556 --> 00:00:30.467
Account contains your profile, settings, and plan.

00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:34.241
Sign in with Apple and finish the short introduction.

00:00:34.241 --> 00:00:37.616
Exploring the app does not start a free trial.

00:00:37.616 --> 00:00:43.615
A trial begins only if Apple offers it, you confirm the subscription, and Rendprop verifies it.

00:00:44.015 --> 00:00:48.081
Open Listings and add the property before making media.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:56.214
The listing is the folder for its original photos, saved edits, videos, website, contact choice, and buyer enquiries.

00:00:56.614 --> 00:00:58.632
Enter the home address carefully.

00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:07.110
Confirm the map suggestion when it is right, then add only facts you know, such as beds, baths, and square feet.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.936
An address can be edited before publishing.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.467
Open Who should buyers contact?

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:17.580
Use your own contact card or select the client’s details when appropriate.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:23.972
Check the visible name, email, and phone before publishing so leads reach the right person.

00:01:24.372 --> 00:01:28.725
Start outside if you have a clear front-of-home photo.

00:01:28.725 --> 00:01:35.013
Then photograph entry, living area, kitchen, bedrooms, baths, and the best outdoor spaces.

00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:40.333
A short, deliberate set is easier to review than many near-duplicates.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.402
Drone-style walkthrough is optional.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:46.991
You can record in the app or upload an existing clip.

00:01:46.991 --> 00:01:51.998
Move slowly and smoothly, keep the phone level, and avoid quick turns.

00:01:51.998 --> 00:01:55.336
The photo-based listing video is a separate feature.

00:01:55.736 --> 00:01:58.238
In the listing toolbox, open Photos.

00:01:58.238 --> 00:02:01.158
Tap Add photos or Take a photo.

00:02:01.158 --> 00:02:08.666
Import keeps the original source, so you can compare every later version and return to the untouched image.

00:02:09.066 --> 00:02:15.057
Use natural light, hold the phone level, and shoot landscape for the website and listing video.

00:02:15.057 --> 00:02:18.801
Use the point-five lens only when the room needs it.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.422
Avoid cutting off walls or important fixtures.

00:02:21.822 --> 00:02:25.419
Tap a photo to inspect its saved versions.

00:02:25.419 --> 00:02:29.466
Switch between Original, Latest, Decluttered, and Staged when available.

00:02:29.466 --> 00:02:36.660
The selected listing version is a choice; creating an edit does not silently replace every photo.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:42.080
From an original, tap the wand or Edit originals with AI.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.732
Choose declutter, staging, sky, or another available edit.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:53.491
Check the credit or plan allowance shown before you start; each selected photo may use AI processing.

00:02:53.891 --> 00:02:56.521
Open the result beside its source.

00:02:56.521 --> 00:03:00.028
Check windows, doors, walls, fixtures, and room proportions.

00:03:00.028 --> 00:03:03.535
A staged room should not invent permanent features.

00:03:03.535 --> 00:03:07.919
Save only edits you would feel comfortable showing a buyer.

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:17.372
Tap a photo’s listing control to use that saved version, or use Select All within a filtered group when the whole set is right.

00:03:17.372 --> 00:03:21.145
Choose a strong cover and review gallery order before publishing.

00:03:21.545 --> 00:03:25.649
Photos can be shared as originals or prepared copies.

00:03:25.649 --> 00:03:29.297
Export photos offers organized versions and destination choices.

00:03:29.297 --> 00:03:37.505
Check your MLS image rules before sending files; website copies are not a substitute for the retained originals.

00:03:37.905 --> 00:03:41.154
Back in the toolbox, tap Make a video.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:46.432
This uses your selected photos to create a downloadable listing or social video.

00:03:46.432 --> 00:03:49.274
It does not require a recorded walkthrough.

00:03:49.274 --> 00:03:52.116
Start with only the strongest reviewed images.

00:03:52.516 --> 00:03:57.326
On Choose your photos, tap images in the sequence viewers should see.

00:03:57.326 --> 00:04:00.532
The numbered tiles show the exact saved versions.

00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:04.139
Change filters if you need originals or finished edits.

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:06.544
Nothing is generated on this screen.

00:04:06.944 --> 00:04:08.633
Choose the look next.

00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:13.699
Wide makes a landscape listing video; Tall makes a vertical social video.

00:04:13.699 --> 00:04:20.031
Pick the destination before checking crop, because the same photo fits differently in each shape.

00:04:20.431 --> 00:04:27.266
In Photo motion, Automatic varies the direction from photo to photo using the four twelve-percent movements.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:34.101
Or choose Push in, Pull back, Glide left, or Glide right to use one direction throughout.

00:04:34.101 --> 00:04:40.936
Set each photo's length: a simple entrance can be brief, while key rooms can hold longer.

00:04:40.936 --> 00:04:42.217
Then preview framing.

00:04:42.617 --> 00:04:45.682
Framing review shows the start and end crop.

00:04:45.682 --> 00:04:48.747
Watch for trimmed ceilings, doorways, or important details.

00:04:48.747 --> 00:04:56.410
If a photo does not fit the format, change the photo or shape before you spend usage on the video.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.209
On the review screen, open Voice and music.

00:05:00.209 --> 00:05:03.183
Music, narration, and large words are optional.

00:05:03.183 --> 00:05:07.007
Preview sound, then pause it before continuing if needed.

00:05:07.007 --> 00:05:11.256
A clean silent video is valid for many listing uses.

00:05:11.656 --> 00:05:15.403
Review the selected photos, timing, and any credit quote.

00:05:15.403 --> 00:05:17.484
Tap Make my video once.

00:05:17.484 --> 00:05:21.648
Processing may take several minutes; you can leave the screen.

00:05:21.648 --> 00:05:24.978
Activity keeps the job under the right property.

00:05:25.378 --> 00:05:28.846
When Activity says Ready, open the finished video.

00:05:28.846 --> 00:05:31.881
Check smoothness, crop, scene order, and sound.

00:05:31.881 --> 00:05:36.215
Save to Photos or Share for MLS or social delivery.

00:05:36.215 --> 00:05:41.417
Tap Use on listing website only after you approve the full video.

00:05:41.817 --> 00:05:46.690
Aerial intro is an optional AI opening shot, not captured drone footage.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:51.156
Use an original photo showing the whole front and actual roof.

00:05:51.156 --> 00:05:56.028
Review the crop, processing terms, and credit quote before making the opening.

00:05:56.428 --> 00:06:02.558
Watch the saved aerial clip and check motion, roof shape, and the path toward the entrance.

00:06:02.558 --> 00:06:06.006
Use as the opening only if you accept it.

00:06:06.006 --> 00:06:10.221
When selected, it plays first; the following photo order stays intact.

00:06:10.621 --> 00:06:15.881
For a separate recorded walkthrough, tag rooms at the moments they appear.

00:06:15.881 --> 00:06:19.388
These become tap-to-jump chapters on the property experience.

00:06:19.388 --> 00:06:24.648
Re-render refreshes that recording; it does not replace the photo-based listing video.

00:06:25.048 --> 00:06:27.742
Open Website design from the listing.

00:06:27.742 --> 00:06:31.334
Classic is the included design with paid access.

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:36.273
Signature Estate and Coastal Luxe are optional property-specific upgrades when available.

00:06:36.273 --> 00:06:39.416
Preview a sample without publishing your draft.

00:06:39.816 --> 00:06:44.980
Check the gallery cover, approved listing video, property facts, address, and buyer contact.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:49.351
The website uses the video you chose as its opening hero.

00:06:49.351 --> 00:06:56.899
If you accepted an aerial opening and included it in that video, it plays first on the website too.

00:06:56.899 --> 00:06:58.885
A recorded walkthrough remains separate.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:02.476
Tap Publish listing when the review is complete.

00:07:02.476 --> 00:07:11.252
Your address-based share link includes a unique publication identifier, so a later agent can publish the same address without taking your page.

00:07:11.252 --> 00:07:14.044
Use Copy, QR, or Share your link.

00:07:14.444 --> 00:07:17.494
The listing also offers an unbranded MLS link.

00:07:17.494 --> 00:07:20.544
Check your local MLS rules before using it.

00:07:20.544 --> 00:07:28.551
Keep the agent-branded share link for your own marketing, and confirm the published page on a browser before sending it broadly.

00:07:28.951 --> 00:07:31.906
Open Leads to see enquiries grouped by listing.

00:07:31.906 --> 00:07:37.078
Follow up from the actual buyer request, and verify the contact method you chose.

00:07:37.078 --> 00:07:41.881
A listing's website can collect enquiries while you work elsewhere in the app.

00:07:42.281 --> 00:07:46.644
Activity groups work as Active, Ready, Needs attention, and History.

00:07:46.644 --> 00:07:50.571
Search for a property when you have many jobs.

00:07:50.571 --> 00:07:54.061
Open a row to return to its listing.

00:07:54.061 --> 00:08:02.787
When completed work can be counted, the app shows a percentage; otherwise it says Progress not reported instead of guessing.

00:08:03.187 --> 00:08:09.457
If a job needs attention, open its listing and read the specific status before retrying.

00:08:09.457 --> 00:08:13.218
Do not repeatedly tap Create or buy credits again.

00:08:13.218 --> 00:08:19.070
Saved photos and requests remain attached to the home; use the offered recovery control.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:24.245
Open Account for Profile and contact card, then Settings and plan.

00:08:24.245 --> 00:08:30.322
Settings includes your app walkthrough, team management when available, account data, and support paths.

00:08:30.322 --> 00:08:34.229
Ask AI can explain the screen you are on.

00:08:34.629 --> 00:08:38.279
Pro, Max, Ultra, and Team are monthly plans.

00:08:38.279 --> 00:08:44.209
Check Apple's current price, included access, and any eligible seven-day offer before confirming.

00:08:44.209 --> 00:08:51.965
The limited trial supports one listing and limited photo edits; video and website publishing need paid access.

00:08:51.965 --> 00:09:00.177
If paid access is missing, select the original workspace and tap Restore purchases in Settings before buying again.

00:09:00.577 --> 00:09:07.483
Credits and extra usage shows the shared workspace balance, monthly and purchased portions, and available top-ups.

00:09:07.483 --> 00:09:09.641
Purchased credits do not expire.

00:09:09.641 --> 00:09:14.388
The app shows a job's credit cost when spending is available.

00:09:14.388 --> 00:09:19.568
If a top-up is missing, tap Check pending purchase before buying again.

00:09:19.968 --> 00:09:24.278
Team workspaces share listing work and one credit balance.

00:09:24.278 --> 00:09:31.462
Owners or admins manage eligible purchases and invitations; seat availability depends on the current subscription.

00:09:31.462 --> 00:09:37.209
Check which workspace is selected before buying or editing a shared property.

00:09:37.609 --> 00:09:48.242
That is the practical path: accurate home details, clean originals, reviewed edits, a video you have watched, the right contact card, and a published website.

00:09:48.242 --> 00:09:54.196
Floor plans and three-dimensional capture are later features, not part of this first release.
